":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Claus Reedtz","key":"sparrevohnpau","last":"Sparrevohn","name":"Sparrevohn, Claus Reedtz","rank":34,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mikael van","key":"deurspau","last":"Deurs","locid":"b53d99e4-6f18-4cd2-add1-c6582f37bd84","name":"van Deurs, Mikael","name_org":"Deurs, Mikael van","orcid":"0000-0003-2368-2502","rank":35,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Rüdiger","key":"vosspau","last":"Voss","name":"Voss, Rüdiger","rank":36,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"53","status":"p"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-0d94d95c-3b52-4d69-a60e-c27bcebfcf7b"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Myfish : Maximising yield of fisheries while balancing ecosystem, economic and social concerns : Legacy booklet","type":"Book","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-308670","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"One of the most important goals in current fisheries management is to maintain or restore stocks above levels that can produce the maximum sustainable yield (MSY). However, it may not be feasible to achieve MSY simultaneously for multiple species because of trade-offs that result from interactions between species, mixed fisheries and the multiple objectives of stakeholders. The premise in this study is that MSY is a concept that needs adaptation, not wholesale replacement. The approach chosen to identify trade-offs and stakeholder preferences involved a process of consulting and discussing options with stakeholders as well as scenario modelling with bio-economic and multi-species models. It is difficult to intuitively anticipate the consequences of complex trade-offs and it is also complicated to address them from a political point of view. However, scenario modelling showed that the current approach of treating each stock separately and ignoring trade-offs may result in unacceptable ecosystem, economic or social effects in North Sea fisheries. Setting FMSY as a management target without any flexibility for compromises may lead to disappointment for some of the stakeholders. To treat FMSY no longer as a point estimate but rather as a “Pretty Good Yield” within sustainable ranges was seen as a promising way forward to avoid unacceptable outcomes when trying to fish all stocks simultaneously at FMSY. This study gives insights on how inclusive governance can help to reach consensus in difficult political processes, and how science can be used to make informed decisions inside a multi-dimensional trade-off space.","author_count":16,"contributors":["Kempf, Alexander","Mumford, John","Levontin, Polina","Leach, Adrian","Hoff, Ayoe","Hamon, Katell","Bartelings, Heleen","Vinther, Morten","Staebler, Moritz","Poos, Jan Jaap","Smout, Sophie","Frost, Hans","van den Burg, Sander","Ulrich, Clara","Rindorf, Anna"],"cuid":["S02-097.04-032647"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany","Netherlands","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Imperial College London","Johann Heinrich von Thunen Institute","Scottish Oceans Institute","Thunen-Institut","University of St Andrews","Wageningen University & Research"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the msy concept in a multi objective fisheries environment lessons learned from the north sea","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.marpol.2016.04.012","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-097.04-032647","identifier":[{"id":"84964318584","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-03357c93-fa0c-4d8e-914f-b886ee20795c","ku-70a6e7de-dbd9-49e8-9b61-cba24d24101d"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-950DCA47E8D1687088417126AFB775B8"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/134786759/Postprint.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.marpol.2016.04.012","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"de","key":"johann heinrich von thunen institute","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Johann Heinrich von Thunen Institute","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"thunen institut","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Thunen-Institut","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"gb","key":"imperial college london","loc":["Unit